{"name":"Heartbreaker","hex":"#cc76a3","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"heartbreaker","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Someone or something that breaks someone's heart, as."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/heartbreaker"}],"entries":[{"title":"Heartbreaker (Mariah Carey song)","blocks":[{"text":"\"Heartbreaker\" is a song by American singer-songwriter Mariah Carey featuring American rapper Jay-Z for her seventh studio album Rainbow (1999). It was released on August 23, 1999, by Columbia Records as the lead single from Rainbow. The song was written by the artists and produced by Carey and DJ Clue, with additional writers being credited for the hook being built around a sample from \"Attack of the Name Game\" by Stacy Lattisaw. \"Heartbreaker\" pushed Carey even further into the R&B and hip hop market, becoming her second commercial single to feature a rapper. Lyrically, the song describes lovesickness towards an unfaithful partner."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/5/5b/Heartbreaker_%28single%29_Mariah_Carey.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Heartbreaker_(Mariah_Carey_song)","wikidata":"Q527927"},{"title":"Heartbreaker (Dionne Warwick song)","blocks":[{"text":"\"Heartbreaker\" is a song performed by American singer Dionne Warwick. It was written by Barry, Robin and Maurice Gibb of the Bee Gees for her 1982 studio album of the same name, and production was done by Barry Gibb, Albhy Galuten, and Karl Richardson under their production name Gibb-Galuten-Richardson. Barry Gibb's backing vocal is heard on the chorus."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/8/8c/Heartbreaker_%28Dionne_Warwick_song%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Heartbreaker_(Dionne_Warwick_song)","wikidata":"Q5692717"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://